# OBS Session Pipeline — environment configuration.
#
# Copy this file to .env in the repo root and edit values for your machine:
#   cp .env.example .env
# .env is gitignored. .env.example ships with safe defaults; if you don't
# create .env, those defaults apply automatically (.env.example is sourced
# as fallback by scripts/_lib.sh).
#
# This file is sourced by bash. Standard KEY=value syntax. Bash variable
# expansion (e.g. $HOME, $WORKSPACE_DIR after it's set above) is supported.
#
# Values set here OVERRIDE any same-named env var in your calling shell.
# This is intentional: edit this file to change settings, rather than
# relying on `export` from your shell rc — config lives in one place.

# ===========================================================================
# Pipeline paths
# ===========================================================================

# Workspace base directory. All data subdirs (recordings/, audio/,
# transcripts/, summaries/) and the per-campaign config/ live under this.
# Most users keep code and data in the same workspace, but you can point
# at a different path (e.g. external drive) here.
WORKSPACE_DIR=$HOME/Movies/OBS

# Where per-campaign data lives (names.txt, name_variants.txt, prompts).
CONFIG_DIR=$WORKSPACE_DIR/config

# ===========================================================================
# Whisper / Ollama models
# ===========================================================================

# Where whisper.cpp .bin models are stored. Change to relocate (e.g. an
# external drive); MODEL_PATH below points at a specific file under it.
WHISPER_MODELS_DIR=$HOME/source/external/whisper_models

# Whisper.cpp model file. large-v3-turbo is several times faster than
# large-v3 with a small accuracy cost. Download from
#   https://huggingface.co/ggerganov/whisper.cpp
# See README "Hardware sizing" for which model fits your RAM.
MODEL_PATH=$WHISPER_MODELS_DIR/ggml-large-v3-turbo-q5_0.bin

# Ollama model tag (after `ollama pull <tag>`). See README "Hardware sizing".
MODEL=qwen2.5:32b-instruct-q4_K_M

# Ceiling on the Ollama context window (input + output tokens). Each request
# is sized to fit its transcript, up to this value; Stage 4 warns if a
# session fills it. Drop to 32768 if you hit out-of-memory; raise if your
# sessions exceed ~3.5 hours. See README "Stage 4".
NUM_CTX=65536

# Seconds to wait for one Ollama reply before giving up on that session.
OLLAMA_TIMEOUT=3600

# Where Ollama is listening. Change if you remote-host it.
OLLAMA_URL=http://localhost:11434

# Spoken language of your recordings. Two-letter ISO 639-1 code (en, es,
# fr, de, ja, etc.). Whisper auto-detects if you set this to `auto`, but
# pinning it avoids occasional misdetection on opening music or silence.
# See whisper.cpp `--help` for the full list.
LANGUAGE=en

# Where Ollama stores its models. NOTE: this only takes effect if exported
# *before* the Ollama daemon starts (the daemon reads it once at boot, not
# per request). To relocate Ollama models — e.g. to a different disk — add
# the same export to your shell rc and restart `ollama serve` /
# `brew services restart ollama`. Setting it here alone is not enough.
# OLLAMA_MODELS=$HOME/.ollama/models

# Same daemon-side rule applies to these two, which shrink the context
# window's memory (KV cache) by about half. See README "Hardware sizing".
# OLLAMA_FLASH_ATTENTION=1
# OLLAMA_KV_CACHE_TYPE=q8_0

# ===========================================================================
# Stage tunables — likely-edited
# ===========================================================================

# Stage 4 (summarize) sampling temperature. Lower = more faithful extraction.
SUMMARIZE_TEMPERATURE=0.3

# Refine pass sampling temperature.
REFINE_TEMPERATURE=0.2

# Stage 3 (cleaner) low-confidence-token threshold. Tokens with whisper
# probability below this get a [?] marker in the cleaned text.
CONFIDENCE_THRESHOLD=0.5

# ===========================================================================
# Advanced — only touch if you know what you're doing
# ===========================================================================
# These tune the whisper.cpp decoder and ffmpeg silence trim. Defaults are
# tested against multi-hour TTRPG recordings; changing them risks worse
# transcription quality, repetition loops, or trimmed dialogue.

# Stage 1 — ffmpeg trailing-silence trim parameters.
# SILENCE_THRESHOLD: anything quieter counts as silence (-40dB default).
# SILENCE_DURATION:  seconds of contiguous silence required before trimming.
SILENCE_THRESHOLD=-40dB
SILENCE_DURATION=10

# Stage 2 — whisper.cpp decoder thresholds.
# WORD_THRESHOLD:    confidence required to emit a timestamp boundary.
# ENTROPY_THRESHOLD: above this, decode is declared failed and falls back.
# TEMPERATURE_INC:   temperature step on each fallback retry.
# THREADS:           CPU thread count (Metal handles the heavy work on
#                    Apple Silicon; this mostly affects pre/post stages).
WORD_THRESHOLD=0.95
ENTROPY_THRESHOLD=3.0
TEMPERATURE_INC=0.5
THREADS=8

# Stage 2 — character budget for the glossary prompt sent to whisper (about
# 200 tokens). whisper keeps at most ~223 prompt tokens. See README "Stage 2".
WHISPER_PROMPT_CHARS=600

# Stage 3 — sliding-window line-level dedupe distance for repetition-loop
# residue. Bump to 16 if longer-cycle loops get through; lower to 4 if
# legitimate repetition is being eaten.
DEDUPE_WINDOW=8
